WEBVTT

00:00.518 --> 00:02.084
- [Voiceover] The
rectangle below has an area

00:02.084 --> 00:05.218
of 12x to the fourth plus 6x to the third

00:05.218 --> 00:08.951
plus 15x squared square meters.

00:08.951 --> 00:10.319
And we can see the area right over here

00:10.319 --> 00:13.084
and they broke it up; this
green area is 12x to the fourth,

00:13.084 --> 00:15.185
this purple area is 6x to the third,

00:15.185 --> 00:16.818
this blue area is 15x squared.

00:16.818 --> 00:19.651
You add 'em all together,
you get this entire rectangle

00:19.651 --> 00:21.818
which would be the combined
area is 12x to the fourth

00:21.818 --> 00:24.718
plus 6x to the third plus 15x squared.

00:24.718 --> 00:26.851
The length of the rectangle in meters,

00:26.851 --> 00:28.384
so this is the length right over here

00:28.384 --> 00:29.617
that we're talking about, so we're talking

00:29.617 --> 00:31.950
about this distance.

00:31.950 --> 00:34.984
The length of the rectangle
in meters is equal to

00:34.984 --> 00:39.818
the greatest common monomial
factor of 12x to the fourth,

00:39.818 --> 00:41.784
6x to the third,

00:41.784 --> 00:45.218
and 15x squared.

00:45.218 --> 00:48.351
What is the length and
width of the rectangle?

00:48.351 --> 00:50.398
I encourage you to pause the video and try

00:50.398 --> 00:52.184
to work through it on your own.

00:52.184 --> 00:54.444
Well the key realization
here is that the length

00:54.444 --> 00:57.551
times the width, the
length times the width

00:57.551 --> 01:00.652
is going to be equal to this area.

01:00.652 --> 01:03.884
And if the length is the
greatest common monomial factor

01:03.884 --> 01:06.151
of these terms, of 12x to the fourth,

01:06.151 --> 01:08.418
6x third, and 15x squared,

01:08.418 --> 01:10.684
well then we can factor that
out and then what we have

01:10.684 --> 01:14.251
left over is going to be the width.

01:14.251 --> 01:16.118
So let's figure out what
is the greatest common

01:16.118 --> 01:17.194
monomial factor

01:17.194 --> 01:21.504
of these three terms.

01:21.504 --> 01:23.218
And the first thing we
could look at is let's look

01:23.218 --> 01:24.584
at the coefficients.

01:24.584 --> 01:26.384
Let's figure out what's
the greatest common factor

01:26.384 --> 01:30.585
of 12, six, and 15.

01:30.585 --> 01:32.218
And there is a couple
of ways you could do it.

01:32.218 --> 01:35.218
You could do it by looking
at a prime factorization,

01:35.218 --> 01:36.984
you could say alright,

01:36.984 --> 01:41.017
well 12 is two times six

01:41.017 --> 01:43.818
which is two times three,

01:43.818 --> 01:45.785
that's the prime factorization of 12.

01:45.785 --> 01:49.451
Prime factorization of six
is just two times three.

01:49.451 --> 01:51.941
Prime factorization of 15

01:51.941 --> 01:56.451
is three times five.

01:56.451 --> 01:58.751
And so the greatest common factor,

01:58.751 --> 02:03.118
the largest factor that's
divisible into all of them,

02:03.118 --> 02:07.684
so let's see, we can
throw a three in there.

02:07.684 --> 02:11.018
Three is divisible into all of them.

02:11.018 --> 02:13.684
And that's it 'cause we
can't say a three and a two.

02:13.684 --> 02:16.751
A three and a two would be
divisible into 12 and six,

02:16.751 --> 02:18.952
but there's no two
that's divisible into 15.

02:18.952 --> 02:21.151
We can't say a three and a five
'cause five isn't divisible

02:21.151 --> 02:24.884
into 12 or six; so the
greatest common factor

02:24.884 --> 02:26.218
is going to be three.

02:26.218 --> 02:27.818
Another way we could have done
this is we could have said

02:27.818 --> 02:31.751
where are the non-prime factors
of each of these numbers.

02:31.751 --> 02:34.084
12 you could have said, OK I can get 12

02:34.084 --> 02:37.551
by saying one times 12

02:37.551 --> 02:41.018
or two times six

02:41.018 --> 02:43.985
or three times four.

02:43.985 --> 02:45.985
Six you could have said,

02:45.985 --> 02:49.884
let's see, that could be one
times six or two times three.

02:49.884 --> 02:51.651
So those are the factors of six.

02:51.651 --> 02:55.518
And then 15 you could have
said well one times 15

02:55.518 --> 02:58.517
or three times five.

02:58.517 --> 03:01.218
And so you say the greatest common factor?

03:01.218 --> 03:04.985
Well three is the largest
number that I've listed here

03:04.985 --> 03:07.784
that is common to all
three of these factors.

03:07.784 --> 03:10.284
So once again, the greatest common factor

03:10.284 --> 03:12.851
of 12, six, and 15 is three.

03:12.851 --> 03:15.051
So when we're looking at the
greatest common monomial factor

03:15.051 --> 03:18.184
the coefficient is going to be three.

03:18.184 --> 03:20.218
And then we look at these powers of X.

03:20.218 --> 03:22.571
We have X to the fourth.

03:23.571 --> 03:25.318
I'm using a different color.

03:25.318 --> 03:27.858
We have X to the fourth,

03:27.858 --> 03:30.478
X to the third, and X squared.

03:30.478 --> 03:31.850
Well what's the largest power of X

03:31.850 --> 03:33.484
that's divisible into all of those?

03:33.484 --> 03:34.585
Well it's going to be X squared.

03:34.585 --> 03:36.117
X squared is divisible
into X to the fourth

03:36.117 --> 03:38.950
and X to the third and of
course X squared itself.

03:38.950 --> 03:42.351
So the greatest common
monomial factor is 3x squared.

03:42.351 --> 03:44.251
This length right over here,

03:44.251 --> 03:47.551
this is 3x squared.

03:47.551 --> 03:49.851
So if this is 3x squared,
we can then figure out

03:49.851 --> 03:52.368
what the width is.

03:52.368 --> 03:57.218
If we were to divide 12x to
the fourth by 3x squared,

03:57.218 --> 03:58.018
what do we get?

03:58.018 --> 04:01.452
Well 12 divided by three is four

04:01.452 --> 04:03.619
and X to the fourth divided by X squared

04:03.619 --> 04:05.485
is X squared.

04:05.485 --> 04:08.051
Notice 3x squared times 4x squared

04:08.051 --> 04:10.218
is 12x to the fourth.

04:10.218 --> 04:12.217
And then we move over
to this purple section.

04:12.217 --> 04:15.385
If we take 6x to the third
divided by 3x squared,

04:15.385 --> 04:18.884
six divided by three is two.

04:18.884 --> 04:21.151
And then X to the third
divided by X squared

04:21.151 --> 04:23.617
is just going to be X.

04:23.617 --> 04:27.718
And then last but not least, we have

04:27.718 --> 04:30.985
15 divided by three is going to be five.

04:30.985 --> 04:32.652
X squared divided by
X squared is just one,

04:32.652 --> 04:33.950
so it's just gonna be five.

04:33.950 --> 04:36.418
So the width is going to be 4x squared,

04:36.418 --> 04:39.251
plus 2x, plus five.

04:39.251 --> 04:42.218
So once again, the length,
we figure that out,

04:42.218 --> 04:45.217
is the greatest common
monomial factor of these terms.

04:45.217 --> 04:47.684
It's 3x squared.

04:47.684 --> 04:50.750
And the width is 4x squared

04:50.750 --> 04:53.584
plus 2x, plus five.

04:53.584 --> 04:56.512
And one way to think about
it is we just factored

04:56.512 --> 04:57.785
this expression over here.

04:57.785 --> 05:01.195
We could write that.

05:01.195 --> 05:03.485
Actually I wanna see the original thing.

05:03.485 --> 05:06.951
We could write that 3x squared

05:06.951 --> 05:09.445
times 4x squared,

05:09.445 --> 05:12.555
plus 2x, plus five

05:12.555 --> 05:14.818
which is the entire width,
well that's going to be

05:14.818 --> 05:16.284
equal to the area.

05:16.284 --> 05:18.385
That's going to be equal
to our original expression:

05:18.385 --> 05:20.484
12x to the fourth power

05:20.484 --> 05:22.751
plus 6x to the third

05:22.751 --> 05:26.132
plus 15x squared.
